> A one-step limit is not a terminal state

A seven-cell corridor starts at3. Either possible first move reaches2 or4, never an endpoint. With time limit1, reward is0, terminated is false, and truncated is true. A learner may bootstrap from the saved final state.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/env_interface_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");e::Corridor env(7,1);env.reset(1);auto r=env.step(1);std::vector<double>values{r.obs[0],r.reward,double(r.terminated),double(r.truncated)};if(r.terminated||!r.truncated||r.reward!=0)return 1;std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/env_interface_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);const double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1e-9,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).title("A one-step limit is not a terminal state").x_label("Coordinate in displayed calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/env_interface_worked.svg");}
